Failed b/w spot allocation and ticket generation

If spot allocation and ticket generation are in the same service/database, you should ideally make them part of one DB transaction:

BEGIN TRANSACTION

1. Allocate spot
2. Create ticket

COMMIT

If ticket creation fails:

ROLLBACK
    ↓
Spot becomes AVAILABLE again

So you get atomicity:

Either both spot allocation + ticket creation happen, or neither happens.




"If ticket generation fails after spot allocation, if both operations are in the same DB transaction,
we roll back the spot allocation. If they're separate services, we release the spot through a compensating action. 
We don't necessarily need idempotency for ticket creation because a new ticket can be generated on retry."


