BestSpotStrategy: How would you efficiently find the best available spot without scanning every spot?
If BestSpotStrategy means nearest spot, I wouldn't scan all 10,000 spots every time.
I would maintain an ordered data structure of available spots:


Floor
  ↓
Available spots ordered by distance from entrance
  ↓
TreeSet / PriorityQueue


For example:
PriorityQueue<ParkingSpot> availableSpots;

Ordered by:
distanceFromEntrance

Then:

poll() → gives nearest available spot
When a vehicle leaves:
release spot
    ↓
add spot back to PriorityQueue


So:
Allocation → O(log N)
Release    → O(log N)

